5. Use Cases
1. HR uploads a CV → gets structured data

Name, email, phone
Skills & technologies
Work experience summary
Languages
Seniority indicators

2. HR uploads/pastes JD → extracts requirements

Required skills
Responsibilities
Minimum experience
Seniority level

3. System evaluates match score

0–100% based on weighted logic
Missing vs. extra skills
Bonus indicators (certifications, languages)

4. System generates candidate summary

3–5 sentence overview
Highlight key strengths
Mention risks or missing pieces

5. HR exports or shares results

JSON
PDF report
API usage (future)


6. Functional Requirements
✅ 6.1 CV Parsing

System must accept PDF and DOCX.
System must extract clean text reliably.
System must parse:

Personal info
Experience (jobs, years)
Hard skills (tech/industry specific)
Soft skills
Languages
Education (optional)



✅ 6.2 JD Parsing

System must accept JD as text input.
Extract:

Required skills
Nice-to-have skills
Seniority
Min. experience
Role responsibilities



✅ 6.3 Matching Logic

Match score 0–100%
Must consider:

Skills overlap
Seniority level
Years of experience
Languages
Missing critical skills


Must output reasoning summary.

✅ 6.4 Candidate Summary

3–5 sentences
Professional tone
Includes:

Core experience
Key skills
Fit assessment
Risks



✅ 6.5 Streamlit UI

CV upload (drag & drop)
JD input (textarea)
“Analyze” button
JSON output block
Match score indicator
Summary display
Error handling

✅ 6.6 API (FastAPI)

/parse endpoint
Accept multipart files + JD text
Return JSON response
Healthcheck endpoint /health


7. Non-Functional Requirements
✅ Performance

Parsing time < 5 seconds
Error rate < 2% for well-formatted CVs

✅ Reliability

Handle CVs 1–5 pages
Handle JD between 2–30 paragraphs
Must degrade gracefully on malformed files

✅ Privacy / Data

No storage by default in MVP
SaaS version: encrypted storage + GDPR compliance

✅ Security

API key required for backend
HTTPS when deployed


8. Technical Architecture Overview
Components:

FastAPI backend (processing, LLM calls)
Parser module (PDF/DOCX parsing)
LLM logic (OpenAI)
Streamlit UI
Deployment (Render, Streamlit Cloud)

Data Flow:
User → Streamlit → FastAPI → CV/JD Parser → OpenAI → Structured Output → Streamlit UI


9. Risks & Mitigation
✅ Risk: LLM hallucinations
Mitigation: structured outputs, controlled prompts, post-processing validation.
✅ Risk: CV formatting inconsistency
Mitigation: fallback regex extraction, multiple extraction passes.
✅ Risk: HR distrust of AI results
Mitigation: provide reasoning + transparent scoring.
✅ Risk: API costs
Mitigation: caching, smaller models, throttling.

